   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Build a regression model using Scikit-learn: prepare and visualize data\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-2-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these Python modules is used to plot the visualization of data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Numpy</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The plots of the pumpkin data are made with Matplotlib, a data visualization library.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Scikit-learn</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Scikit-learn is used to build machine learning models. Plotting is done with Matplotlib.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Matplotlib</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Matplotlib is a data visualization library that works well in Jupyter notebooks.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-2-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>If you want to understand the spread or the other characteristics of data points of your dataset, then perform:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Data Visualization</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Plots and charts show different aspects of your data, like relationships and gaps that are hard to see otherwise.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Data Preprocessing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Preparing data gets it ready for building a model. To see the spread and other traits of data, you plot it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Train Test Split</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. To see the spread and other traits of your data, you make plots, graphs, and charts. That is data visualization.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-2-2-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of these is a part of the Data Visualization step in a Machine Learning project?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Incorporating a certain Machine Learning algorithm</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Plots can help you pick an ML technique, but the visualization step itself is making the plots.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Creating a pictorial representation of data using different plotting methods</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data visualization means making plots, graphs, and charts that show different aspects of the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Normalizing the values of a dataset</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Normalizing values, like pricing per bushel, is part of preparing the data, not visualizing it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
